1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,469
Noon.

2
00:00:01,469 --> 00:00:03,646
500 seats go on sale

3
00:00:03,646 --> 00:00:05,400
and 3,000 people press

4
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,958
Buy within three seconds.

5
00:00:07,958 --> 00:00:10,487
Over 2,000 checkouts fail.

6
00:00:10,487 --> 00:00:12,959
And the shop sells 875 seats.

7
00:00:12,959 --> 00:00:15,037
375 of them don't exist.

8
00:00:16,562 --> 00:00:17,688
Here's the checkout that did it.

9
00:00:17,688 --> 00:00:20,433
It reads the seats left, then writes

10
00:00:20,433 --> 00:00:21,961
in two separate queries.

11
00:00:21,961 --> 00:00:24,310
Thousands of buyers read "seats

12
00:00:24,310 --> 00:00:26,375
left" before anyone writes

13
00:00:26,375 --> 00:00:27,962
so they all get a seat.

14
00:00:27,962 --> 00:00:30,175
And everyone else waits for a database

15
00:00:30,175 --> 00:00:31,812
connection until it times out.

16
00:00:32,744 --> 00:00:35,782
The fix: a waiting room in front of the shop.

17
00:00:35,782 --> 00:00:37,119
Buyers without a pass go to

18
00:00:37,119 --> 00:00:39,594
Hibira's hosted waiting page.

19
00:00:39,594 --> 00:00:40,944
They take a number and watch

20
00:00:40,944 --> 00:00:42,519
their place move live.

21
00:00:42,519 --> 00:00:44,244
Then they're let in a few at a time

22
00:00:44,244 --> 00:00:45,519
each with a signed pass.

23
00:00:46,442 --> 00:00:48,738
Step one: create the room.

24
00:00:48,738 --> 00:00:51,461
One signed request with the Pusher library.

25
00:00:51,461 --> 00:00:52,542
Let in 1,200 people a minute

26
00:00:52,542 --> 00:00:54,692
and send them back to the drop page.

27
00:00:55,580 --> 00:00:57,955
Step two: protect the page.

28
00:00:57,955 --> 00:00:59,430
expressWaitingRoom checks

29
00:00:59,430 --> 00:01:01,855
the pass on every request.

30
00:01:01,855 --> 00:01:02,943
No pass?

31
00:01:02,943 --> 00:01:03,993
Off to the queue.

32
00:01:03,993 --> 00:01:06,468
With a valid pass, the drop page loads.

33
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:09,657
Step three: fix the checkout.

34
00:01:09,657 --> 00:01:11,745
Check and take a seat in one step

35
00:01:11,745 --> 00:01:14,295
so no seat is sold twice.

36
00:01:14,295 --> 00:01:16,207
Each queue number buys once.

37
00:01:16,207 --> 00:01:19,007
And when the last seat goes, close the room

38
00:01:19,007 --> 00:01:21,582
so everyone still in line hears it right away.

39
00:01:22,484 --> 00:01:24,321
Now the same 3,000 buyers again.

40
00:01:24,321 --> 00:01:25,984
The laptop takes a number

41
00:01:25,984 --> 00:01:27,646
and watches the line move.

42
00:01:27,646 --> 00:01:30,901
Its turn comes, and the seat is secured.

43
00:01:30,901 --> 00:01:32,449
The phone arrived later.

44
00:01:32,449 --> 00:01:35,271
It sees right away that the room is closed.

45
00:01:37,170 --> 00:01:38,758
Exactly 500 seats sold.

46
00:01:38,758 --> 00:01:42,583
None oversold, and not one failed checkout.

47
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:47,400
The full example is linked in the description.

48
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,575
Start free at hibira.io.

